{
  "case_id": "2008-06-11206",
  "document_hash": "48bc969b22153ab9c35ba1bb797f0e9e923ce70127c7249a2ca1117afb27463f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Robert N. Hochman)",
      "case_id": "2008-06-11206",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48bc969b22153ab9c35ba1bb797f0e9e923ce70127c7249a2ca1117afb27463f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48bc969b2215-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Failure to report is not a violent felony under the Armed Career Criminal Act because it presents neither a serious potential risk of injury to others nor involves violent and aggressive conduct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-06-11206",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48bc969b22153ab9c35ba1bb797f0e9e923ce70127c7249a2ca1117afb27463f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48bc969b2215-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: There is really a problem about -- about what you suggest. It may destroy the whole benefit of the categorical approach."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-06-11206",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48bc969b22153ab9c35ba1bb797f0e9e923ce70127c7249a2ca1117afb27463f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48bc969b2215-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Isn't that a separate question? If it had -- if it has to be found by a jury, it can be submitted to the jury?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Roberts (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2008-06-11206",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48bc969b22153ab9c35ba1bb797f0e9e923ce70127c7249a2ca1117afb27463f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48bc969b2215-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Failure-to-report escape qualifies as a violent felony under the ACCA's residual clause because it creates a serious potential risk of physical injury that's comparable in both kind and degree to the risk that's created by the enumerated offense of burglary."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-06-11206",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48bc969b22153ab9c35ba1bb797f0e9e923ce70127c7249a2ca1117afb27463f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48bc969b2215-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Roberts, wouldn't that be so of any crime? This is failure to report. Any crime, any -- an arrest for any crime has a certain risk that the arrestee is going to resist. Is there anything different, is anything greater, about this arrest for this kind of crime?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-06-11206",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48bc969b22153ab9c35ba1bb797f0e9e923ce70127c7249a2ca1117afb27463f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48bc969b2215-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Say that again. I didn't understand it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Roberts (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2008-06-11206",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48bc969b22153ab9c35ba1bb797f0e9e923ce70127c7249a2ca1117afb27463f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48bc969b2215-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "escape inherently avoids -- inherently involves the avoidance of custody and custody is the very obligation that recapture is trying to impose."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-06-11206",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48bc969b22153ab9c35ba1bb797f0e9e923ce70127c7249a2ca1117afb27463f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48bc969b2215-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But would the statute apply if -- say he is supposed to go in on the weekends. Instead, he goes out on a binge, and then he voluntarily comes in on a Monday morning saying, yes, I failed to report, and so here I am."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-06-11206",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48bc969b22153ab9c35ba1bb797f0e9e923ce70127c7249a2ca1117afb27463f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48bc969b2215-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is the magnitude of the risk relevant? Suppose it happens one out of 10,000 times or 99 out of 100 times. Are they different cases?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-06-11206",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48bc969b22153ab9c35ba1bb797f0e9e923ce70127c7249a2ca1117afb27463f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48bc969b2215-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But your argument goes simply to whether there is potential and the statute says \"serious potential.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Roberts (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2008-06-11206",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48bc969b22153ab9c35ba1bb797f0e9e923ce70127c7249a2ca1117afb27463f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48bc969b2215-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's a 3.1 percent -- 3.1 percent rate of having this dangerous weapon when he is being -- being taken into custody for -- for this offense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-06-11206",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48bc969b22153ab9c35ba1bb797f0e9e923ce70127c7249a2ca1117afb27463f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48bc969b2215-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I -- may I -- may I ask you just to get some sense about what will qualify?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hochman",
      "case_id": "2008-06-11206",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "48bc969b22153ab9c35ba1bb797f0e9e923ce70127c7249a2ca1117afb27463f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-48bc969b2215-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Just to begin with where Mr. Roberts left off, most states in fact do distinguish in their statutes between failure to report and prison break escapes. These are cited by both parties in the briefs and you can review them, but there are clear distinctions in the law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-06-11206",
      "confidence": 0.0,
